{
  "description": "GB throughput-scale base: one causally-coupled market with a 30-agent heterogeneous ecology (NoiseTrader/MarketMaker/ValueTrader/MomentumTrader) over a 30s horizon, driving ~68k events at ~20k events/sec. Each GB unit scales a single throughput axis (population, horizon, per-agent arrival rate, order-size intensity, oracle-jump volume, or mixed-density) while remaining ONE coupled market that must reproduce its own fill sequence exactly. A static-batched / vmap-over-books port that shares state across books, homogenizes the pairwise latency draw, or reorders the causal event queue to win aggregate events/sec fails per-scenario Tier-A (exact fill sequence + Kendall-tau >= 0.999).",
